# Test: fib kernel beside fib vpp validates under interface backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze config validate` accept `fib kernel` alongside `fib vpp`
#           under `interface backend vpp`?
#           A unit test cannot prove `fib-kernel`'s `HostSideDataPlane` mark
#           reaches `ze config validate` through the real composition root.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-14 (C-3a) -- `fib kernel`
#            marks itself host-side (programming the Linux route table for the
#            router's own traffic) and validates beside `fib vpp` under VPP.
# PREVENTS: breaking the documented dual-FIB VPP deployment ("To run both,
#           write both").
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
fib {
	kernel {
	}
	vpp {
		enabled true;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid
